students from Stoneman Douglas High  School are returning to class today you  can see students arriving for a half day  of modified classes two weeks after they  fled from a gunman on campus 17 students  and staff members were killed on that  Valentine's Day the school district says  there is now enhanced security at the  school but they are not giving any  specifics the massacre led survivors and  students from all over the US to  organize a call for tougher gun control  laws Adriana Diaz spoke to students and  teachers ahead of Stoneman Douglas High  School's reopening she is outside the  school in parkland Florida  Adriana good morning good morning both  students and teachers are anxious about  going back to school today and one  teacher told us that grief counselors  will be in the classrooms of victims who  passed away to provide support for  survivors I think everyone's a little  bit nervous ago it's gonna be a huge  just rush walking in returning to school  was all 15-year old sophomore Liam  Kernan could think about as he ate  dinner with his family last night but he  says he's not afraid actually tomorrow  is the beginning of change and we will  be the people to do it  Liam along with more than 3,000 other  Stoneman Douglas students will attend a  half-day of 24 minute classes extra  security and counselors will be on hand  we just aren't quite sure yet what the  new normal is ap psychology teacher Lisa  Chauvin has taught at Stoneman Douglas  for 26 years we're not really sure what  to expect because everyone is coming  with a different experience  some students were directly involved in  the events of that day  we're all human we're all in this  together and we're going to go through  the process of healing together building  12 the crime scene is blocked off by a  fence covered with posters of support no  one will be allowed inside the school  board wants it torn down and a memorial  built in its place I'm just hoping it's  gonna be a normal day but I think  there's gonna be a somber mood senior  anisha Sarah Polley  lost her close friend Carmen Sentra in  the Valentine's Day Massacre she'd  always brightened everyone  J'son now you know she's not here I'm  still trying to fight the fact that this  happened because I'm still in disbelief  what's her school mascot the Eagles you  can't say that without smiling I mean  it's such a good mascot for us honestly  I mean maybe a Phoenix would have been  better since out of the ashes we rise  and at this point I've never been  prouder to me an eagle today is anita's  17th birthday she told us she's thankful  there's no lunch period so she doesn't  have to sit without her friend Carmen  the school returns to a full day of  classes next week Gail thank you
 

